# GlassBar, GlassToolbar

> Lede 0.7.0's docs for GlassBar, GlassToolbar, installed with it. Setup, and every item in the release: [README.md](README.md). Online: https://lede.cloudcompute.com/reference/glass-bar.md

GlassBar, a `<nav>` of links between places that marks the current one with `aria-current`, and GlassToolbar, a Base UI Toolbar of actions, both on glass. GlassToolbarButton and GlassToolbarSeparator fill the toolbar.

## Install

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add @lede/glass-bar
```

The command needs Lede's registry in `components.json`, as [README.md](README.md#use-it-in-a-shadcn-project) shows. It also installs the items [`lede-theme`](lede-theme.md) and [`lede-utils`](lede-utils.md), and the npm packages `@base-ui/react@^1.9.0`. The item's JSON, with each file's source, is https://lede.cloudcompute.com/r/v0.7.0/glass-bar.json.

## Import

```tsx
import { GlassBar, GlassToolbar } from '@/components/lede/glass-bar';
```

## Files and exports

| Installs to | Import from | Exports |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `components/lede/glass-bar.tsx` | `@/components/lede/glass-bar` | `GlassBar` (component), `GlassToolbar` (component), `GlassToolbarButton` (component), `GlassToolbarSeparator` (component), `GlassBarItem` (type), `GlassBarProps` (type), `GlassToolbarProps` (type), `GlassToolbarButtonProps` (type) |

## GlassBar props

Navigation between places: a `<nav>` and a `<ul>` of real links, or of buttons for client routing, with `aria-current`. HTML attributes and `ref` go on the `<nav>`.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `aria-label` (required) | `string` |  | Accessible name of the navigation landmark. |
| `items` (required) | `GlassBarItem[]` |  |  |
| `value` | `string` |  | The current place, marked with `aria-current="page"`. With a router, pass the item for its location, so Back and Forward move the mark too. Without `value` or `defaultValue`, link items mark the one whose `href` is the page's path as it mounts, or none, and button items mark the first. |
| `defaultValue` | `string` |  |  |
| `onValueChange` | `(value: string) => void` |  |  |
| `placement` | `'inline' \| 'top' \| 'bottom'` | `inline` | `'inline'`, or fixed at the top or bottom center of the viewport. Default `'inline'`. |

GlassBar also takes the attributes of `<nav>`, such as `className`.

## GlassToolbar props

Actions on the current view: a Base UI Toolbar (`role="toolbar"`, roving arrow-key focus) on glass.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `aria-label` (required) | `string` |  | Defines a string value that labels the current element. |
| `placement` | `'inline' \| 'top' \| 'bottom'` |  |  |
| `className` | `string` |  |  |

GlassToolbar also takes the props of `Toolbar.Root` from `@base-ui/react/toolbar`, such as `aria-describedby`.

## Example

The smallest working use, from the docs site:

```tsx
import { GlassBar, GlassToolbar, GlassToolbarButton } from '@/components/lede/glass-bar';

export function PhotoChrome({ current, onShare }: { current: string; onShare: () => void }) {
  return (
    <>
      <GlassBar
        aria-label="Sections"
        placement="bottom"
        value={current}
        items={[{ value: 'home', label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { value: 'library', label: 'Library', href: '/library' }]}
      />
      <GlassToolbar aria-label="Photo tools" placement="top">
        <GlassToolbarButton onClick={onShare}>Share</GlassToolbarButton>
      </GlassToolbar>
    </>
  );
}
```

